{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And they shall set its staves.</b> What is stated [elsewhere], 'they shall not be removed from it' — there were four staves: two fixed in it, and concerning them it says 'they shall not be removed from it,' and concerning the two others it says 'and they shall set its staves.' Another interpretation: there were only two staves there, but there were two grooves in the staves, and they would place the rings into the grooves so that the ark would not fall on the one walking first when descending, nor on the one walking last when ascending. Another interpretation: <b>and they shall set its staves</b> upon the shoulders of the carriers."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:25.970251523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}